# Source preparation

See [the retained handler boundary](../../base/rag/indexer/README.md). Only the saved-HTML command is integrated into the documented pack build workflow; other handlers remain candidates for extraction or deletion.

Preserve locators, original hashes, attribution and reviewable source text. For a new local command, require an explicit root and file selection, reject symlinks/traversal, bound input/output and publish privately without overwriting files. Acquire remote content only through a separately reviewed, bounded contract.

Do not restore queue workers, model enrichment, database writers or scheduled jobs because a retained helper once used them. Retain helpers only for an actual preparation need. A content heuristic or metadata label cannot establish truth, authorization or safe execution.
